    "1. Identify bias and argument in texts.\n2. Evaluate the effectiveness of an argument.\n3. Answer analytical comprehension questions.",
    "ANALYSING ARGUMENTATIVE TEXTS\nAn argumentative text presents a position and attempts to convince the reader.\n\nSTEPS TO ANALYSE\n1. Identify the claim/thesis.\n2. Identify the evidence used.\n3. Assess the quality of evidence.\n4. Identify counter-arguments and how they are handled.\n5. Evaluate: Is the argument convincing? Why/Why not?\n\nQUESTION TYPES\n• 'What is the author's main claim?' — State thesis.\n• 'What evidence supports the author's view?' — Quote and explain.\n• 'Do you agree with the author?' — State position, give reasons.\n• 'Evaluate the effectiveness of the argument.' — Strengths and weaknesses.",
